== 3.6 Chapter 3 Practice Drill — 40 Questions

40 questions graded in the order the CBT engine is likely to meet them. Allow 44 minutes; the key and a full solution for every question follow.

#mcq(1, [Job costing is most suitable for a firm that],
  [bakes bread in identical batches],
  [mines coal],
  [refines crude oil continuously],
  [makes furniture to individual customers' orders]
)

#mcq(2, [Batch costing is used where],
  [the product is a service only],
  [identical units are produced in groups],
  [each unit is unique],
  [production is continuous]
)

#mcq(3, [Which industry is most likely to use process costing?],
  [cement manufacture],
  [audit practice],
  [house construction],
  [shipbuilding]
)

#mcq(4, [A job cost card contains all of the following EXCEPT],
  [direct materials issued],
  [the firm's advertising cost],
  [direct labour booked to the job],
  [absorbed production overhead]
)

#mcq(5, [The overhead in a job cost card is],
  [the selling overhead],
  [the actual overhead of the year],
  [an absorbed figure at a predetermined rate],
  [always equal to the direct labour]
)

#mcq(6, [A batch of 500 units costs ₦30,000 and 20 units are rejected. The cost per good unit is],
  [₦57.69],
  [₦60.00],
  [₦62.50],
  [₦64.00]
)

#mcq(7, [The effect of rejected units on the cost of the good units is to],
  [increase it],
  [reduce it],
  [leave it unchanged],
  [make it equal to prime cost]
)

#mcq(8, [The debit side of a process account contains],
  [the abnormal gain],
  [the output transferred out],
  [the normal loss],
  [material, labour, overhead and any opening work in progress]
)

#mcq(9, [Normal loss is loss which],
  [arises from an accident],
  [occurs only at the year end],
  [is caused by carelessness],
  [cannot be avoided in the normal course of the process]
)

#mcq(10, [The scrap value of normal loss is],
  [ignored],
  [charged to the profit and loss account],
  [deducted from the cost before computing the unit cost],
  [added to the cost of the process]
)

#mcq(11, [Cost per unit in a process is computed as],
  [total cost ÷ normal loss units],
  [total cost ÷ input units],
  [(total cost − scrap value of normal loss) ÷ expected output],
  [total cost ÷ output units]
)

#mcq(12, [Input 1,000 units costing ₦6,000; normal loss 25 per cent; no scrap value. The cost per unit is],
  [₦8.00],
  [₦6.00],
  [₦7.50],
  [₦9.00]
)

#mcq(13, [Input 1,000 units costing ₦7,000; normal loss 25 per cent, sold as scrap at ₦4 a unit. The cost per unit is],
  [₦6.40],
  [₦9.33],
  [₦8.00],
  [₦7.00]
)

#mcq(14, [Using the last figures, actual output was 700 units. The abnormal loss is],
  [nil],
  [100 units, ₦800],
  [50 units, ₦350],
  [50 units, ₦400]
)

#mcq(15, [An abnormal gain is],
  [credited in the process account and debited to profit and loss],
  [ignored in the process account],
  [added to the cost of good output],
  [debited in the process account and credited to profit and loss]
)

#mcq(16, [In a process account, the two sides must agree in],
  [value only],
  [neither],
  [units only],
  [both units and value]
)

#mcq(17, [An equivalent unit is],
  [a unit transferred to the next process],
  [the work content of a partly finished unit expressed as a complete unit],
  [a unit that has been sold],
  [a unit of normal loss]
)

#mcq(18, [Closing work in progress is 400 units, 25 per cent complete. The equivalent units are],
  [300],
  [25],
  [100],
  [400]
)

#mcq(19, [In process costing, the cost transferred from process I to process II is],
  [a normal loss],
  [an expense of process II],
  [a material cost of process II],
  [a fixed overhead]
)

#mcq(20, [Closing work in progress in a process account is],
  [debited to the process account],
  [credited to the process account and carried forward],
  [written off to profit and loss],
  [ignored]
)

#mcq(21, [The sale of factory scrap is],
  [debited to the process account],
  [added to the cost of production],
  [treated as sales revenue],
  [credited to the process or manufacturing account]
)

#mcq(22, [An increase in the normal loss percentage, with the same total cost, will],
  [leave it unchanged],
  [make the process break even],
  [reduce the cost per good unit],
  [increase the cost per good unit]
)

#mcq(23, [If actual output equals expected output, the process account will show],
  [an abnormal loss],
  [neither an abnormal loss nor an abnormal gain],
  [an abnormal gain],
  [a normal loss only]
)

#mcq(24, [Contract costing differs from job costing because a contract],
  [is carried out on the customer's site and lasts longer],
  [has no direct labour],
  [never uses material],
  [is smaller than a job]
)

#mcq(25, [Which firm would NOT use process costing?],
  [a brewery],
  [a firm of accountants preparing a client's accounts],
  [a flour mill],
  [a sugar refinery]
)

#mcq(26, [In process costing, abnormal loss is valued at],
  [the input price per unit],
  [the cost per good unit],
  [nil],
  [scrap value]
)

#mcq(27, [An abnormal gain is credited to the],
  [profit and loss account],
  [manufacturing account],
  [revaluation account],
  [capital account]
)

#mcq(28, [Input 2,000 units at a cost of ₦12,000, with no loss. The cost per unit is],
  [₦5.00],
  [₦6.00],
  [₦4.00],
  [₦12.00]
)

#mcq(29, [Normal loss and abnormal loss are distinguished by whether the loss is],
  [valued or unvalued],
  [sold or unsold],
  [expected or unexpected],
  [large or small]
)

#mcq(30, [Closing work in progress is valued at],
  [equivalent units × cost per unit],
  [its selling price],
  [the scrap value],
  [the cost of the input only]
)

#mcq(31, [A job's prime cost is ₦40,000, overhead is absorbed at 20 per cent of prime cost, and the firm adds a 10 per cent mark-up on total cost. The price quoted is],
  [₦52,800],
  [₦44,000],
  [₦48,000],
  [₦50,000]
)

#mcq(32, [The document that records the material issued to a particular job is the],
  [purchase order],
  [stores requisition],
  [clock card],
  [goods received note]
)

#mcq(33, [In a process account, the units credited must equal the units],
  [debited],
  [produced plus losses and closing work in progress],
  [transferred],
  [sold]
)

#mcq(34, [When there is an opening work in progress, the equivalent units of the period are reduced by],
  [the whole of the opening work in progress],
  [the closing work in progress],
  [the work already done on the opening units last year],
  [the normal loss]
)

#mcq(35, [A firm producing paint in 500-litre batches would most likely use],
  [job costing],
  [process costing],
  [contract costing],
  [batch costing]
)

#mcq(36, [The cost of a normal loss that has no scrap value is],
  [written off to profit and loss],
  [borne by the good units],
  [carried forward as stock],
  [debited to the trading account]
)

#mcq(37, [Which statement about abnormal loss is correct?],
  [It is expected and absorbed into unit cost],
  [It increases the cost of the good units],
  [It is always valued at scrap value],
  [It is unexpected and written off to profit and loss]
)

#mcq(38, [In a process account, work in progress appears],
  [only as a closing balance],
  [only as an opening balance],
  [as an opening balance and as a closing balance],
  [not at all]
)

#mcq(39, [The principal advantage of process costing is that it],
  [prices each customer's order separately],
  [values stock at selling price],
  [avoids the need for any overhead absorption],
  [produces an average cost per unit for a continuous stream]
)

#mcq(40, [In a process with a normal loss that has scrap value, the cost of the lost units is],
  [written off to profit and loss],
  [recovered in full from the scrap sale],
  [carried forward as work in progress],
  [partly recovered, and the rest is borne by the good units]
)

